<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lika</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lika is a mountainous region of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, between the Velebit range and the Bosnian border, with Gospić as its main town. In antiquity it was home to the Iapydes. Later it was a frontier between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> and Ottoman empires and part of the Military Frontier; it includes part of Plitvice Lakes National Park.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lika.jpg" alt="Lika" width="320" height="313" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LandGrey · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lika_i_Li%C4%8Dko_primorje.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
